WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.667
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.033
and Golden Globe-winning
comedian

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.934
you know from his work
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:07.601
"Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"
"Palm Springs,"

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.534
and as one third
of The Lonely Island.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:13.000
New episodes of his animated
series "Digman!" per-- per--

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.167
premiere -- oh, my God --
premiere Wednesday nights

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:16.434
at 10:30 on Comedy Central.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.801
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.267
our very good friend
Andy Samberg.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:29.868
♪♪

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:37.167
♪♪

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:44.501
♪♪

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:46.968
Welcome back, my friend.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.234
What a reaction.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:52.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.367
-This is a big deal.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.267
It has been a while since
you've been here in person.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:57.567
And, in fact, the last time
you were here in person,

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.968
we were doing a cast show
for "Brooklyn Nine-Nine,"

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.834
the series finale
of "Brooklyn Nine-Nine."

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.133
-That's right.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.033
-And the night before,
we were supposed to have dinner,

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:07.834
me, you, and Shoemaker, and I
called you guys and I said,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.167
"I can't go to dinner because
Alexi just went into labor,"

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.567
and we had a baby girl
that night.

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:16.501
Now, there was a fear
that I wouldn't be able

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.234
to come and host the show
the next day.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.067
But your whole cast
had flown out.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:22.067
We knew we had to do the show.
You were gonna host the show.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.868
-Yes, I got a call
from Shoemaker being like,

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.467
"Hey, will you host
the show tomorrow?"

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.067
I said, "Of course."

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:30.234
Easy-peasy.
I was all excited.

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.934
I got all this stuff prepped.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.033
-Oh, you prepped things
for hosting the show?

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.367
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:37.734
I mean, truth be told,

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.834
I've kind of had my eye
on it for a while.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.601
-Like, to take over?

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.133
-Yeah, it was --

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:49.467
it was, like, kind of a hostile
takeover I had planned.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:52.000
And then I was all, "Here's
my moment ready to seize."

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.334
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.667
So what sort of planning
had you put into this?

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.367
-I had full segments
planned out.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:00.167
-Oh, really? And you weren't
gonna use existing segments?

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:01.834
-No, no, no.
I was gonna blow that all up.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:03.434
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:06.534
-All-new brand-new material.

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.200
-Inspired by anything?

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.634
-Nope.
-Totally unique?

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:12.934
-Yep, just original --
original ideas that I had.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.300
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.067
-You want to share any?
-I mean, yeah.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:18.133
It looks like you're
not gonna leave, so...

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:23.234
...I guess I'll just burn them.

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:26.300
Okay, here's a couple of ideas
I had that I was gonna try out.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.501
-Okay.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:30.367
-One of them was called
"Jokes Andy Can't Tell."

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.300
-Okay. So, now,
we do have a segment

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.601
called "Jokes Seth Can't Tell."

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.400
-Yeah, but this is different.
-Okay.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.834
-Yeah.
-What's this one?

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.300
-So it would be like a series
of jokes that I can't tell.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.634
But it's not because
they're inappropriate.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.400
It's because
they all contain words

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.300
that I don't know
how to pronounce.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.234
-Oh, so you have to, like,
bail on them

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.667
'cause you just can't do it.
-Yeah, it would be like,

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:53.968
"What's the deal with
wors-i-sis-shire sauce?"

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.300
You know?

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.534
And then, like, goofy jokes
like, you know,

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.667
what did one sea en-a-manem-ony

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:03.834
say to the -- while
it was eating a "gy-ro"?

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.801
-You can't say "gy-ro"?

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:10.701
-You say it.
-Alright. "Hee-ro."

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.534
-"Yee-ro."
-Oh, well there you go.

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:13.834
So you can tell it.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:16.467
-Broke the fourth wall.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.300
-Any other ideas?
-Oh, God. So many.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.901
So, yeah, I had another idea
called "Guess What I Ate,"

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.868
where I take a bite of food

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.934
and then a celebrity guest
smells my breath

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.968
and they guess what I ate.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.701
-I don't think people
would like that.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.667
-No, they would've liked it.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:35.000
And then I had another one
called "Should I Be Worried?"

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.033
And that would be I would invite
a dermatologist on the show

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:41.501
and show them all of my moles

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:44.968
and then after each one
be like, "Should I be worried?"

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.367
-And you think that would be
something, like,

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:47.567
people at home would enjoy?

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:50.033
-Oh, it would have been
on a T-shirt in no time.

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:52.267
Yeah.
What else?

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:57.000
Oh, I had another one where
famed cue card holder Wally

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.701
and I just gently kiss
for two minutes.

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:00.267
-Okay, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:03.100
-Yeah. So that's like
a time filler.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.033
-Yeah.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.133
What's that?

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:10.667
-I'm sorry. Are you saying you
can't hear over the applause?

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:11.834
-I couldn't hear
over the applause, yeah.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:14.400
-Okay, gotcha.
Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.100
-Anyway, that one's
self-explanatory.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.534
And then I had another one
called "Punch or Hug."

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:21.667
-Okay.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.534
-And I would just
go through the audience

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.133
and give each person
the opportunity

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.667
to either punch or hug me.

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:28.100
-Okay.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.734
-And honestly, Seth, that one,
it's like whatever they feel

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:33.367
that they most need
for their emotional health.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.567
You know, I'm just happy
to be of service.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.200
-That's very modern.
Yeah.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.834
-Yeah. Let's see.

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:41.801
Oh, I also had a desk piece
that I tested out in my mind

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.400
called "The Spitroast,"

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.701
where I just eviscerated
newsworthy topics

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:46.901
straight to their face.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.000
-Well, that's kind of similar
to "Ya Burnt,"

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.801
which is a segment we have.
-What's that?

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:53.634
-Well, that's --
that's my sketch I do.

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:56.467
It's a sketch called "Ya Burnt,"
where we roast people,

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.300
you know, things.
-I don't know what that is,

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.968
but it sounds bad,
but this idea was a good idea.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.801
Here, I'll show you.
Take a look.

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.701
[ Sizzling ]

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.767
Welcome to the barbecue pit...

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.334
where we've got a bunch
of suckling little piggies

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:17.367
and one long spit
to roast them on.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.634
First up, the Charmin bears.

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:22.267
Hey, Charmin bears, I think
you need to see a doctor.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:27.033
Nobody's supposed to spend
that much time in the bathroom.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:30.300
IBS is a disease,
not a personality.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:34.234
Also, I've never seen
any of you wash your hands.

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:36.200
You guys are [bleep] gross.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.367
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.567
Yeah.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:43.167
If you knew how goddamn
disgusting you sounded

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:45.834
talking about [bleep]
all the time,

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:47.334
you'd put a gun in your mouth

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:50.834
and blow
your [bleep] brains out.

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:53.801
Hey, Charmin bears, time to take
the apple out of your mouth,

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:56.133
because ya spit-roasted.

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:57.367
[ Sizzling ]

00:05:57.367 --> 00:05:59.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:03.133
Yeah.

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:05.067
-Like, it sort of started

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:06.567
with some details
about the Charmin bear.

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.267
Then it just got,
like, really --

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.200
You, like, really
went at them hard.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.634
-Yeah, well, you know,
I don't pull punches.

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:14.701
-Also, that is totally
the same thing as "Ya Burnt."

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:16.067
-Yeah, again,
I don't know what that is.

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:17.634
"Ya Blurt."
What --

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:19.300
What words are you even saying?

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.033
To me it sounds like gibberish.

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:24.234
-I should just move on.
Do you have another?

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:26.567
-It's funny you ask,
'cause I do have one more.

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:28.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.501
And I think we have time.
-Okay. Yeah.

00:06:30.501 --> 00:06:31.934
So you'd be very good
at this job,

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.901
'cause a lot of it is knowing
whether or not there's time.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:35.267
Knowing, like, "Oh,
we got to go to commercial

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:37.367
'cause they pay the bills."

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:38.801
You know?
-Don't say that.

00:06:38.801 --> 00:06:40.133
Peek behind the curtain.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.300
No big deal.
That's free of cost.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.868
So, okay, you know
how you do "A Closer Look"?

00:06:43.868 --> 00:06:45.534
-I do, Yeah.
-Pbht!

00:06:45.534 --> 00:06:48.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:50.200
The thing that you --

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.534
The thing that you olds
don't understand about...

00:06:52.534 --> 00:06:56.100
-Olds?
-...about my online generation

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.434
is that we don't have
the attention span

00:06:58.434 --> 00:07:00.133
for a 45-minute deep dive

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:02.300
into triangular arbitrage
or whatever.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:03.601
-Uh-huh. Yeah.

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:06.701
First of all, you're like
only five years younger than me.

00:07:06.701 --> 00:07:07.801
-Really?

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:09.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.200
Man, you should moisturize more.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:15.167
So that's a harsh burn.

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:17.400
-I got spit-roasted.
-You got spit-roasted.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.467
Where's the camera?
Spit-roasted.

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:21.868
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:24.467
-Anyways, instead of
"A Closer Look,"

00:07:24.467 --> 00:07:27.067
I would take a grosser look.

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:29.367
-Okay.

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:31.868
-Seth's nightmare-inducing
hell spawn Frisbee

00:07:31.868 --> 00:07:34.834
continues to maintain
its identity as a dog

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:39.801
when it's clearly some sort
of rat-foreskin hybrid.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:42.400
For more on this, it's time
for "A Grosser Look."

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:53.367
This is a dog.

00:07:53.367 --> 00:07:55.434
This is not a dog.

00:07:55.434 --> 00:07:57.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.934 --> 00:08:01.100
This is the worst greyhound
since the bus.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:06.601
If this dog took a dump,
I wouldn't know which was which

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:09.000
and flush them both
down the toilet.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.133
[ Toilet flushes ]

00:08:13.734 --> 00:08:15.334
This has been "A Grosser Look."

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:17.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:27.133
-We'll be right back with more
from Andy Samberg.

